From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Wed, 27 Nov 2013 16:10:51 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] est.map multicore
Message-ID: <DSmH7vNmHv4.0rkev6nzxE0J@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <DSmH7vNmHv4.pl5G0U8eujEJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <DSmH7vNmHv4.na-3RuUk6l0J@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com> <DSmH7vNmHv4.pl5G0U8eujEJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/DSmH7vNmHv4/m/0rkev6nzxE0J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What's going on is that for 5 of your 6 chromosomes, the estimated map is derived almost instantly, and the 6th (chromosome 4) takes a very long time.  Since the parallel analysis is to have each CPU work on one chromosome, you don't get any advantage. You see six processes spawned but 5 of the 6 finish almost instantly.

karl

